		'Split: keys.ts holds every key decision (key, edit, recall, paste, and the Target/KeyInput types); app.ts keeps state, host events and sending, and never imports keys.ts (keys imports app). Chat.tsx builds the Target from the DOM (coarse from matchMedia, links count as buttons, anything inside an open <dialog> as a field) and prevents the default when keys says so.',
		'Typing anywhere: keys.key calls keys.insert(e.key) for one-code-point keys without Ctrl/Alt/Cmd when the target is not a field (Space on a button or link stays native); Composer points keys.insert at editor.write on the textarea, so the key lands at the saved caret, on the undo stack, once (the default is prevented). A document paste listener does the same through keys.paste (attach.paste first). The CDP test checks it with a real Input.dispatchKeyEvent after blur(): synthetic KeyboardEvents never type text.',
